WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.575
Your Conditional Access policies
already require a compliant device.

3
00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:09.624
That's only as good as Intune's
compliance records, and by default,

4
00:00:09.624 --> 00:00:13.750
a device with no compliance policy
assigned counts as compliant.

5
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.962
Microsoft recommends changing
that to not compliant,

6
00:00:16.962 --> 00:00:19.388
and targeting every device with a policy.

7
00:00:19.388 --> 00:00:24.282
The workbook's device evidence guidance
asks for evidence a script can collect:

8
00:00:24.282 --> 00:00:28.287
which devices fail which policy,
which devices no policy reaches,

9
00:00:28.287 --> 00:00:32.811
which stopped checking in, which aren't
encrypted or are below the OS floor,

10
00:00:32.811 --> 00:00:36.149
and which Autopilot registrations
won't get a profile.

11
00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:39.421
The validation kit already
has six Intune checks,

12
00:00:39.421 --> 00:00:43.650
reading Entra device objects,
group tags and assignment design.

13
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.500
This module doesn't repeat them.

14
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.980
Its checks read Intune's own records.
